content:
{
  "asset": "P-112 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow has fallen about 20% over two weeks at unchanged valve settings. The applicable documented flow/head value is the HF-300 rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m; this is a rating, not a documented minimum-flow, alarm, or trip limit. Because no absolute initial/final flow or head is reported, a numeric acceptance comparison cannot be made. The symptom does match the manual's 'Low flow or head' troubleshooting entry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable manufacturer vibration criterion is Figure 3, for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported 2.0 mm/s was measured on that basis, it lies in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS), below the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary. It is not in the highest severity zone, Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS on the shown axis), so the site immediate-stop rule is not triggered. The report does not specify RMS or measurement location, so that basis must be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the manual's bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, the reported housing temperature of 65 C is within the normal range, which extends up to 70 C. It is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Consequently, it does not trigger the site requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift, which applies when temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller is the first internal cause to investigate because the manual specifically associates it with low flow or head; inspect the wear rings at the same time. The gradual flow loss is consistent with investigating wear, but the report does not confirm it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in the suction is the next documented cause to check because it can produce low flow or head without a change in valve settings. The manual's corrective action includes venting the casing and reassessing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A closed valve remains a documented possible cause, but is less likely than on a changed-lineup report because the valve settings are reported unchanged. Verify the actual valve lineup rather than assuming the settings prove the flow path is correct.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, record absolute flow and head and verify the valve lineup. Check for air in the suction, vent the casing as the manual's low-flow troubleshooting action, and reassess flow. Also confirm that the vibration reading is mm/s RMS on a bearing housing so that Figure 3 can be applied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If low flow persists and internal inspection is required, isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain the line-break permit after draining and venting before starting work inside the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly for inspection; its rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment required for components over 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the impeller and wear rings and record their condition. Do not authorize impeller or bearing replacement solely from the present flow report: the troubleshooting manual requires inspection, and no impeller/wear-ring acceptance limits are supplied in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is authorized after inspection, remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450; HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting, although the scoring inspection is still required. Fit a new casing gasket whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten disturbed Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm, where applicable. For HF3-450B seal gland nuts, use 30 Nm under SB-2026-014; do not use the manual's superseded 25 Nm value for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the work moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment after reassembly. Accept only parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before running, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. After reinstatement and venting, verify flow/head against the recorded baseline and recheck vibration and housing temperature. Stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart if vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone; raise a priority-1 work order within the shift if bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; quantity one if the casing is opened. The parts manual requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; conditional on seal replacement being authorized. Required instead of HF3-450 for this serial range; do not stage HF3-450 as the replacement seal.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part if the withdrawn sleeve has scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth. Inspection must determine whether it is actually fitted.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the site's 25 kg lifting threshold. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are mandatory.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Verify whether P-112 is on chemically dosed service before starting. Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory for chemically dosed lines; the supplied dosing statement specifically identifies P-101 to P-106, not P-112, so it does not by itself establish that requirement for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry, including during recommissioning after any seal or internal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current readings do not require an immediate stop. If subsequent vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Base diagnostic/back pull-out inspection labour cannot be quantified from the evidence. Table 6 provides no standard time for troubleshooting, venting, back pull-out inspection, or impeller/wear-ring inspection, so no inspection hours are guessed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement allowance, only if that repair is authorized: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. The service bulletin alone does not establish that the non-leaking installed seal must be replaced proactively.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser-alignment allowance if the motor or bearing housing is moved: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies HF3-450 as the component mechanical seal, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and to use HF3-450B instead. P-112 is serial HF3-22300, so the serial-specific bulletin applies and HF3-450B governs any replacement seal for this asset. The bulletin does not itself mandate replacement of an installed seal that has not been condemned.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual Table 5 and the general seal procedure give/use 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because HF3-22300 is within the bulletin's HF3-22000-and-above range, use 30 Nm with HF3-450B on P-112; the other applicable Table 5 torques remain unchanged.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What are the actual initial and current flow and head, the required process minimum, and the production consequence of the 20% loss? C02 gives only rated duty, not a low-flow acceptance band or priority rule; these details are needed to confirm the provisional P2 priority and post-work acceptance criterion. [C02]",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration reading recorded as RMS velocity on a bearing housing, and at what measurement point? Figure 3's zone classification applies only on that stated basis. [C07]",
    "What are the impeller and wear-ring wear limits, required clearances, and wear-ring part details? C09 requires inspection, while C05 lists impeller HF3-210 but supplies no wear acceptance criteria or wear-ring part number. [C05, C09]",
    "Is seal replacement actually in the authorized scope, which seal is presently installed, and is there any sleeve scoring? C13 prohibits fitting HF3-450 on this serial but does not explicitly order proactive replacement of a non-leaking installed seal. [C13]",
    "What fluid line serves P-112, and is it chemically dosed? C16 documents dosing only for P-101 to P-106; if P-112 is also dosed, C15 requires chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. [C15, C16]",
    "What labour and outage allowance should be assigned to diagnosis and inspection, and will the final scope include seal, impeller, or bearing work? C12 contains standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement, and laser alignment, not for the base inspection. [C12]"
  ]
}
